{"id":"leetcode-439","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Ternary Expression Parser","summary":"Given a string expression with nested ternary conditions, evaluate the expression and return the result.","statement":"Given a string expression with nested ternary conditions, evaluate the expression and return the result. The expression uses 'T' for true, 'F' for false, and digits for numbers. Conditions group right-to-left, and the result is a digit, 'T', or 'F'.","constraints":["5 <= expression.length <= 10,000; input is a valid ternary expression using T,F,?,:, and single decimal digits.","Conditions are T or F; branches may be nested. Group conditional expressions right-to-left.","Return one character as a string: a digit, T, or F. Do not use Python truthiness of the character F."],"topics":["strings","stacks","recursion"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"evaluate_ternary","parameters":[{"name":"expression","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"str","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def evaluate_ternary(expression: str) -> str:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def evaluate_ternary(expression):\n    stack = []\n    for char in reversed(expression):\n        if stack and stack[-1]=='?':\n            stack.pop()\n            yes = stack.pop()\n            stack.pop()\n            no = stack.pop()\n            stack.append(yes if char=='T' else no)\n        else:\n            stack.append(char)\n    return stack[-1]\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def evaluate_ternary(expression):\n    return expression[2] if expression[0]=='T' else expression[-1]\n","def evaluate_ternary(expression):\n    stack = []\n    for char in reversed(expression):\n        if stack and stack[-1]=='?':\n            stack.pop()\n            yes = stack.pop()\n            stack.pop()\n            no = stack.pop()\n            stack.append(yes if bool(char) else no)\n        else:\n            stack.append(char)\n    return stack[-1]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["A branch may itself be an entire conditional expression.","Scan from right to left so nested branch results are ready before their condition.","On a condition before ?, pop the reduced true and false branches and push the selected value; otherwise push the token.","Each token is pushed and popped at most once. An explicit stack supports thousands of nested conditions without recursive evaluation."],"editorial":"Right-to-left scanning respects right association. When a condition is encountered, its two branches have already collapsed into single results, so selection is local. Keep T/F as literal characters and test equality with T; both strings are truthy in Python. Return the final character, preserving boolean-looking results as strings.","tests":[{"id":"lc-439-1","arguments":["T?2:3"],"expected":"2","comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"T chooses the true branch, so return the string \"2\".","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-2","arguments":["T?T?F:5:3"],"expected":"F","comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The true branch is T?F:5, which evaluates to F. The outer true condition therefore returns \"F\".","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-3","arguments":["F?1:T?4:5"],"expected":"4","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-4","arguments":["F?2:3"],"expected":"3","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-5","arguments":["T?0:9"],"expected":"0","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-6","arguments":["F?T:F"],"expected":"F","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-7","arguments":["T?T:F"],"expected":"T","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-8","arguments":["T?1:F?2:3"],"expected":"1","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-9","arguments":["F?T?1:2:3"],"expected":"3","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-10","arguments":["F?0:F?1:T?2:3"],"expected":"2","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-11","arguments":["T?F?1:2:3"],"expected":"2","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-12","arguments":["T?9:0"],"expected":"9","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-13","arguments":["F?9:T"],"expected":"T","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-14","arguments":["T?F?T:F:F"],"expected":"F","comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-439-stress-1","arguments":["F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0:F?0: